// S. Prince Management Tool: Prisma schema (Phase 1 + core platform; Phase 2/3 tables included, no screens yet).
// Source of truth for the data model. Summary and conventions: docs/data-model.md.
//
// Conventions
//  - IDs: String cuid by default; seed rows use readable ids (reg_cg, stg_won, ...).
//  - Money Decimal(14,2); quantities Decimal(14,3); percentages Decimal(7,4).
//  - Pure dates are @db.Date, timestamps are UTC.
//  - Business tables carry createdAt/updatedAt/createdById/updatedById/deletedAt/version
//    (createdById/updatedById are plain strings = users.id, not FKs, so audit columns never block a user change).
//  - Business-unique keys on soft-deletable rows (tenderNo, project code, invoiceNo, gstin, ...) are NOT declared here:
//    Prisma cannot model partial indexes (it reports them as drift), so they exist only as
//    "UNIQUE ... WHERE deletedAt IS NULL" indexes in the hardening migration. Look rows up with findFirst({ deletedAt: null }).
//  - Append-only tables (AuditLog, ApprovalAction, TenderStageHistory, SecurityInstrumentEvent) have no soft delete/version;
//    the DB blocks UPDATE/DELETE on AuditLog and ApprovalAction by trigger (raw SQL migration).
//  - Scope columns (regionId, projectId, siteId) are denormalised on transactional tables for scoped queries.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

